{{!--
  Override of the nav-tree partial of ui-bundle.zip (the original is unchanged except for the marked lines).
  It renders the top-level navigation groups of every component expanded by default (the top-level list
  is wrapped in an untitled list at depth 0) and, inside the "Open Source Projects" group, the project groups too, so all projects and all guide sections are visible
  without clicking.
  It also emits only the levels a reader needs, so the nav does not repeat the whole subtree of every section in
  every page (that made guide pages over 1 MB). The child list of an entry is rendered only when the entry is at
  depth 0 or 1 (so the groups and the sections are listed), or contains the current page (computed once per entry by the
  nav-item-state helper, ui-overrides/helpers/nav-item-state.js), or was opened by its parent (an untitled list wrapper or
  "Open Source Projects"), or is a text-only group heading (an entry with children and no url). Other subtrees are not in the
  HTML (and get no toggle button); readers reach them through the entry's own link (its index page). A text-only heading
  has no page, so it is never pruned: its children are emitted with a toggle, collapsed unless the current page is in
  them (pruning it left the heading as a dead end, #394). The bundle's own toggle buttons and the "toggle all" button keep working because they only
  toggle the is-active class that is rendered here. The entries on the path to the current page are rendered with
  is-active, so the ancestors of the current page are open.
--}}
{{#if navigation.length}}
<ul class="nav-list">
  {{#each navigation as |item|}}
  {{!-- WP2/WP3: open and expand state computed once per entry (see the header comment and the helper) --}}
  {{#with (nav-item-state item ../level ../open @root.page.url) as |s|}}
  <li class="nav-item{{#if s.current}} is-current-page{{/if}}{{#if s.active}} is-active{{/if}}" data-depth="{{s.depth}}">
    {{#if item.content}}
    {{#if s.toggle}}
    <button class="nav-item-toggle"></button>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if item.url}}
    <a class="nav-link" href="
      {{~#if (eq item.urlType 'internal')}}{{{relativize item.url}}}
      {{~else}}{{{item.url}}}{{~/if}}">{{{item.content}}}</a>
    {{else}}
    <span class="nav-text">{{{item.content}}}</span>
    {{/if}}
    {{/if}}
{{!-- WP3: emit the child list only when needed; WP2: an untitled wrapper and "Open Source Projects" open their children --}}
{{#if s.expand}}
{{> nav-tree navigation=item.items level=s.childLevel open=s.openChildren}}
{{/if}}
  </li>
  {{/with}}
  {{/each}}
</ul>
{{/if}}
